=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play ssh/alpine323 -------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
# Play mode, mocks: the SSH Login screen proposed for slice 6,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host (the SSH$
# checks, sshd.ReadEffective, migrate.Find, users.Read,$
# revert.ReadSession), each change the real steps.PlanSSH or$
# PlanMigration on the real plan/apply engine. The lockout$
# checks before asking are the gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s$
# to build. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's.$
$
# Info: ssh/alpine323$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.23 (OpenSSH 10.2p1, OpenRC,$
# sshd without PAM). As the VM: 50-cloud-init.conf refuses$
# passwords; root "!" with a key, so root can't log in at all;$
# george "*" in wheel, doas nopass; no ufw.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root locked$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [ ] SSH Port             Not Configured default (22)$
$
# SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Locked root's account, no PAM$
   -  Password Login       Off by 50-cloud-init.conf$
   -  SSH Port             22$
   -  Allowed Users        Anyone$
   -  Logged in as         george, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disallow root login  Root can't log in over SSH$
   2) Password login on    Let passwords log in again$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 3$
$
# Change SSH port ##############################################$
$
  New SSH port [0 or q]: 2230$
$
# SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  SSH Port             22 held until confirmed$
$
   -  Install hardn's boot unit$
      /etc/init.d/hardn-boot$
      @@ -0,0 +1,23 @@$
      +#!/sbin/openrc-run$
      +# hardn's boot service (P-34 (c);$
      | docs/safety/revert-boot.md). hardn installs$
      +# it before it arms the revert timer of a change that$
      | could lock you out, and$
      +# removes it at a boot that finds no change journalled.$
      +#$
      +# At boot, before sshd starts: re-arm the revert timer of$
      | a change waiting$
      +# for "hardn confirm", for what remains of its window, or$
      | roll the change$
      +# back when its deadline has passed. Ordering only: sshd$
      | starts whatever$
      +# this service does.$
      +$
      +description="hardn: re-arm or run the revert timer of an$
      | unconfirmed change"$
      +$
      +depend() {$
      +    need localmount$
      +    after bootmisc firewall$
      +    before sshd$
      +}$
      +$
      +start() {$
      +    ebegin "hardn: checking the change journal"$
      +    /usr/local/bin/hardn rollback --boot$
      +    eend $?$
      +}$
      -not installed$
      +installed and enabled$
      $ sh -n /run/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx/hardn-boot$
      $ rc-update add hardn-boot default$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Add SSH port 2230$
$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
      @@ -0,0 +1,4 @@$
      +# Managed by hardn.$
      +# Set by hardn:$
      +Port 22$
      +Port 2230$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      Reload sshd (openrc sshd)$
$
      sshd$
      $ rc-service sshd reload$
$
  [ ] Lockout risk$
      sshd -T shows ports 22, 2230$
$
      sshd -T$
      $ sshd -T$
$
  Change the SSH port?$
$
  Type the hostname [web-01, 0 or q]: web-01$
$
  [+] Install hardn's boot unit     Done$
  [+] Add SSH port 2230             Done$
  [+] Reload sshd (openrc sshd)     Done$
  [+] sshd -T shows ports 22, 2230  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# Warning$
# This change reverts automatically in 3:00$
# To keep it, open a new SSH session on port 2230 and run:$
$
      $ doas hardn confirm$
$
  Unless confirmed, change 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx is rolled$
  back at about 12:03:00 UTC. To undo it now, run doas hardn$
  rollback 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx.$
$
# SSH Login ####################################################$
$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root locked$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [ ] SSH Port             Partial 22 and 2230$
$
# SSH Configuration --------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Root SSH Login       Locked root's account, no PAM$
   -  Password Login       Off by 50-cloud-init.conf$
   -  SSH Port             22, 2230$
   -  Allowed Users        Anyone$
   -  Logged in as         george, by key$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disallow root login  Root can't log in over SSH$
   2) Password login on    Let passwords log in again$
   3) Change SSH port      Now 22 and 2230$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: ssh/alpine323$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Install hardn's boot unit$
      /etc/init.d/hardn-boot$
      $ rc-update add hardn-boot default$
$
   -  Armed the revert timer$
      $ /bin/sh -c "sleep \"$1\" && \"$0\" rollback \"$2\""$
      | /usr/local/bin/hardn 180 20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
   -  Applied: Add SSH port 2230$
      /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
$
   -  Applied: Reload sshd (openrc sshd)$
      $ rc-service sshd reload$
$

